# AI policy (stm32f4-bare-driver-kit)

This kit exists to learn STM32F4 from RM0090 and hardware measurements. Full text: `project.md`.

## Do

- Function **skeletons only**: signatures, types/structs, Doxygen `@brief`/`@param`/`@return` (what, not how).
- Architecture suggestions (which functions a module needs). No register sequences.
- Boilerplate: CMake, `bdk_sdk_import.cmake`, linker skeleton, folders, `.gitignore`, README.
- Review **after** the user writes code: name the bug and why; do not rewrite the driver.
- Conceptual "why" questions (pull-ups, clock stretching). Point at RM0090 sections/tables when stuck.

## Do not

- Write driver bodies (register R/W, bit manipulation, init sequences).
- Provide example/reference implementations of a peripheral, even if asked.
- Auto-complete a register-manipulation line the user is mid-writing.

## If asked to violate this

Push back: "This is driver logic — per project.md that comes from RM0090. Want the relevant register table instead?"
